    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "38 Pembroke Road is a substantial four-storey over lower ground period townhouse, set within a fine brick terrace on one of Ballsbridge’s best-known residential roads. The house presents behind a classic Dublin 4 facade, a slate roof, sash windows and a decoratively panelled front door beneath a fanlight, approached over granite steps and behind cast iron railings.\r\n\r\nThe building has been in commercial use for a number of years, currently arranged as office accommodation across the hall, first and second floors, with a self-contained apartment at lower ground floor level. Full planning permission has been granted (Dublin City Council Reg. Ref. WEB1757/26, granted 1st July 2026) to change the use of the building back to residential and reconfigure the accommodation into a generous four/five bedroom family home extending to approximately 327.3 sq m / 3,523 sq ft, with the benefit of a private, gated parking courtyard to the rear.\r\n\r\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial Dublin 4 property with the planning work already done, in one of the city’s most established and sought-after residential locations."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Full planning permission granted for change of use to residential (Ref. WEB1757/26, granted 01/07/2026)\r\nApprox. 327.3 sq m / 3,523 sq ft gross internal area\r\nProposed four/five bedroom accommodation, four with en suite bathrooms\r\nPrivate, gated parking courtyard to the rear with electric gates\r\nEnclosed courtyard garden \r\nPeriod features retained: brick facade, slate roof, sash windows, cornicing, original staircase\r\nFour floors: lower ground, ground, first and second\r\nPrime Ballsbridge / Pembroke Road address,"
      },
      {
